{"type":"npc","name":"Puddle Hopper","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":75,"temp":0,"max":75,"details":""},"ac":{"value":20,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":30}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":5,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"fire","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["fey","thalassic"],"details":""},"level":{"value":4},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Puddle hoppers enjoy resting with their disproportionately long limbs hidden under the water's surface, pretending to be nothing more than typical giant frogs. Then, they wait for someone to pass by before emerging from the puddle to reveal their true height. Often, the shock causes travelers to flinch and flee, much to the delight of the puddle hopper. If the travelers drop something interesting while they run, so much the better.</p><p>Puddle hoppers are avid collectors, and they have no qualms about nabbing anything they find that strikes their interest. They usually keep to unattended objects left out in the open far from civilization. In addition to gathering the dropped belongings of the people they scare, puddle hoppers collect other objects that have been left behind in remote areas. In contrast to their normal behavior, they can become particularly bold in times of heavy rain as large puddles fill settlements; they use this opportunity to seek out even more intriguing things that other people own. Due to their aquatic nature, the majority of their thefts are things people left outside their homes, with wind chimes and birdhouses being favorites. However, a few unfortunate incidents have occurred in homes where puddle hoppers accidentally mistake full baths for some sort of small ponds.</p><p>They particularly enjoy looting waterlogged homes; families returning after evacuating from a flood might find a seemingly random collection of their belongings gone.</p><h2>Equivalent Exchange</h2><p>Though not particularly brilliant, puddle hoppers aren't unreasonable and are sometimes willing to trade their pilfered goods for items they regard to be of equal or greater value. What constitutes a fair trade, however, varies from one hopper to another. Whereas one puddle hopper might trade a precious gemstone for a bit of interestingly shaped crystal, another might regard a relatively worthless bauble as a priceless treasure and demand nothing less than a king's ransom for it!</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 12/27/50 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Deception, Intimidation, Stealth, Thievery)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (fire, vitality), mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), space, space shield, strength, water, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Austin Smith","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":1},"int":{"mod":-1},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":12,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":12,"special":[]},"deception":{"base":10,"special":[]},"intimidation":{"base":10,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":10,"special":[{"label":"when in water","predicate":["terrain:water"],"base":12}]},"thievery":{"base":12}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious","fey","water"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}}